-> Each name is bound once at top level. This isn't a convention — it's
-> checked. Writing `a = 1` again after `a` already has a value is an
-> error ("variables are single-assignment"), never a silent overwrite.
a = 1
b = a + 1
assert b = 2

-> Because names never change out from under you, `b` above is settled the
-> moment it's written. Reassignment is allowed in exactly one place — the
-> inside of a handler body — covered in 05-handlers.
